  "plain": "After airmen at Ellsworth Air Force Base in South Dakota reported a strange encounter in 1977, their Air Force interrogators are said to have spent most of their time trying to explain the experience away, and the men faced demotions and denial. Michels tells this himself, framing the story of two of the witnesses, an airman named Mario Woods and a fellow airman named Michael. He says that what hurt most was not the event but how they were treated afterwards."
